 the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 1 of 12 months; January fell. Highs rose in 5 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Elkins' yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.03 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 47.1 inches a year. The wettest year was 1996 (72.88 in); the driest, 1930 (28.38 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 11 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}